    "witness:7": {
      "end": 1023,
      "quote": "The checkout page already contains a working payment button. The existing flow is complete and functional:\n\n- `web/index.html` includes a `<form id=\"checkout-form\">` with a payment method `<select>` (card / bank_transfer) and a submit button `<button type=\"submit\" id=\"pay-button\">Pay now</button>`.\n- `web/app.js` wires that button to the existing checkout flow: on submit it disables the button, shows \"Processing payment...\", POSTs the cart and selected method to `/api/checkout`, then renders either the payment status/amount or a failure message, and re-enables the button.\n- The backend `Handler.do_POST` in the server routes `/api/checkout` to `create_checkout`, which validates the cart and method and returns `{status, amount_cents, method}`.\n\nNo code changes were required: the payment button is already present and correctly integrated with the existing checkout flow. If you intended a *new* button (e.g., a separate \"Pay with card\" quick-pay button distinct from the form submit), let me know and I can add it.",
      "read_id": "read:8",
